Data that is not part of this repository

  The tracking models in models/ (except the eye model) are made from
  upstream files by research/ tools and keep their own licenses.

Models the tracking core uses, all commercially usable

  MediaPipe Face Landmarker   Google, Apache-2.0
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/face_landmarker/
    The face_landmarker.task bundle holds the face detector, FaceMesh-V2 and
    Blendshapes V2. Yorishiro changes their format, not their weights:
    - face detector: tflite2onnx to ONNX, then pnnx to ncnn
      (research/tools/export_mediapipe.py, a channel Pad op is rewritten
      for ncnn).
    - FaceMesh-V2: the ONNX conversion from PINTO model zoo 410_FaceMeshV2
      (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/PINTO0309/PINTO_model_zoo), then pnnx
      to ncnn.
    - Blendshapes V2: converted to ONNX by research/tools/mixer_tflite_to_onnx.py
      (fp16 weights stored as fp32, 1x1 convolutions as MatMul).
    Training data per Google's model cards: FaceMesh-V2 on Google's own
    smartphone photos taken through an AR app, depth from synthetic data;
    Blendshapes V2 on samples generated from multi-view lab captures fitted
    with Google's GHUM face model. The data is not distributed.
  MediaPipe Hand Landmarker   Google, Apache-2.0 (hand tracking, optional)
    https://storage.googleapis.com/mediapipe-models/hand_landmarker/
    The hand_landmarker.task bundle holds the palm detector and the hand
    landmark model. Converted, weights unchanged: tflite2onnx and tf2onnx to
    ONNX, pnnx to ncnn (research/tools/export_hands.py).
  ICT-FaceKit                 USC Institute for Creative Technologies, MIT
    https://github.com/ICT-VGL/ICT-FaceKit
    Neutral head and 53 ARKit-named expression shapes, used by the expression
    solver (models/core/fit.npz, research/tools/export_fit.py) and the
    preview avatar.
  Eye openness model          Yorishiro, Apache-2.0
    models/eye_openness.onnx, part of this repository. Trained only on
    synthetic renders of the ICT-FaceKit head (research/tools/eye_synth),
    eye crops located by FaceMesh-V2. No photos of
    real people were used for training; the user's own clips and CREMA-D were
    used for evaluation only.

Code adapted from MediaPipe (Apache-2.0)

  crates/tracking/src/smooth.rs follows MediaPipe's
  LandmarksSmoothingCalculator and OneEuroFilter and uses the Face
  Landmarker's smoothing settings. crates/tracking/src/inference.rs
  reimplements MediaPipe's face detector decoding and landmark ROI handling
  and copies the landmark subset and output order of
  face_blendshapes_graph.cc, crates/tracking/src/hands.rs its palm detector
  decoding and hand crops, research/src/yorishiro_research/mediapipe_ncnn/
  the face part in Python. Copyright Google LLC, Apache-2.0.

Evaluation only, not used by the tracker and not distributed

  OpenSeeFace (BSD-2-Clause) and Intel Open Model Zoo models (Apache-2.0)
  were run in their own environments for comparison (tools in git history).
  Research datasets (for example CREMA-D, ODbL) are used for evaluation only,
  never for training. Hand tracking is evaluated on a sample of HaGRID
  (CC BY-SA 4.0), also never for training.
  Live2D sample models and the Live2D Cubism SDK are not included and are not
  redistributed. Users download them and accept Live2D's terms themselves.
  Yorishiro renders Live2D models with Katashiro (from Ayagami) and does not ship Live2D Cubism
  Core.

